{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And they went up from about, etc. and Dathan and Abiram came out, etc.</b> The verse informs us of the obstinacy of the kelipot, that even after they saw that Israel feared for themselves lest the evil that would befall Dathan and Abiram cling to them, nevertheless they came out standing defiant. From this Moses was roused and said <b>by this you shall know</b>, etc. — meaning, since he saw that Dathan and Abiram were not moved by the reaction that Israel had demonstrated by withdrawing from around them, but on the contrary came out with upright posture, Moses concluded in his mind with certainty that the wicked in their malice think that Moses does these things of his own devising through stratagems and cunning — telling them to move away so that they would see and be dismayed, and not by the word of HaShem. Therefore he said <b>by this you shall know that HaShem has sent me to do all these deeds</b> — meaning, even these particular details. And he stipulated that besides their dying, still further they would die an unusual death unlike any other deaths, as will be explained further on."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:25.206868099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}